\f0\b\fs30 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 \cb2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 1. How should one approach the E-news Express project?
\f1\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs32 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 \cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Before starting the project, please read the problem statement carefully and go through the criteria and descriptions mentioned in the rubric.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Once you understand the task,\'a0download and import the dataset into a jupyter notebook to get started with the project.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 To work on the project, you should first start with an exploratory data analysis\'a0followed by\'a0descriptive statistics and visualization to understand the data.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Once the EDA is completed, you can use the data to start answering the business problem that we are trying to address.\'a0It is important to close the analysis with key findings and recommendations to the business.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb2 \strokec3 \'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 2. Is it necessary\'a0to get a random sample from the dataset to perform the tests?\'a0
\f1\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 No, you should assume that the dataset is a simple random sample from the population, and the sample observations are independent of each other.\
\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 3. Does\'a0this project require the same level of extensive visualizations and EDA as the previous project?
\f1\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 You are expected to perform basic dataset exploration, univariate analysis, bivariate analysis, missing value check, etc. Though it is similar to the\'a0previous project, the level will vary as the dataset is very different for this project. However, please be sure to provide the observations/insights from your analysis as given in the\'a0previous\'a0project.\
\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 4. What kind of visuals are expected to be performed to describe the hypothesis testing questions?
\f1\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 You are expected to use visual analysis for comparison of the data that will be used in hypothesis testing. For example, boxplot() can be used to compare the means in an ANOVA test. Similarly, you can draw any suitable plot to find visual evidence against your formulated hypotheses.\'a0You can use boxplot, barplot, or any other suitable plot depending upon the type of data used in the test.\
\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 5.\'a0 How to calculate the conversion rate?
\f1\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 Conversion rate is the proportion of users who visit the landing page and get converted. For example, if out of 50 users, 20 gets converted. Then the conversion rate is 20/50 =0.4\
\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 6.\'a0Is it necessary to follow both the rejection region Approach and p_value approach for the Hypothesis testing?
\f1\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 It is not necessary to follow both the\'a0rejection region approach and p-value approach for the hypothesis testing. You can use either of them (preferably the p-value approach) to get the inference. The rejection region approach might be a bit lengthy and can take more time as compared to the p-value approach.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
